  <!-- Latin Empire of Constantinople (Culture.empire, Kingdom.empire_w) troop tree - own ids,
       own upgrade chain, own equipment, distinct from crusader_custom_troops.xml (Levantine
       Crusader States) and byzantine_custom_troops.xml (Bizans). Every item id verified against
       SandBoxCore/ModuleData/items/*.xml. Tier structure (6/11/16/21/26/31) and skill totals
       (90/195/360/508/676/835) match this mod's audited standard.
       Historical grounding: Genoese/Pisan crossbow mercenaries were central to the 1204 siege of
       Constantinople; Vlach horsemen served as Balkan light cavalry auxiliaries to the Latin
       Empire; Gasmouloi (mixed Greek-Latin soldiery, unique to Frankokratia-era Greece) as the
       infantry's elite endpoint; "Baron of Romania" as the top knightly rank, the real feudal
       title used by the Latin Empire's great vassals under the 1204 Partition Treaty. Horses use
       the empire_horse line (locally sourced in Thrace) rather than vlandia_horse, and armor
       blends Western knightly weapons with Constantinople-made helms/lamellar, keeping the tree
       visually distinct from the Crusader States' purely Frankish-Levantine look. -->

